Description: CVE-2026-28859 - Fix use-after-free in GPU-process glyph drawing
 The GPU process handler RemoteDisplayListRecorder::drawGlyphs passed the
 IPC-supplied glyph and advance spans (ArrayReferenceTuple, backed by shared
 memory the web process controls) directly into WebCore's drawGlyphs. A
 compromised web process could mutate or free that backing store while the GPU
 process was still reading from it, producing a use-after-free (CWE-416).
 .
 Backport of WebKit bug 308248 (upstream commit
 3e59292b95de1c22169fc939999ddd84d746319e, which fixed the identical code in
 RemoteGraphicsContext::drawGlyphs after that method was refactored out of
 RemoteDisplayListRecorder). Copy both the glyph span and the advance span into
 local Vectors (inline capacity 128 to limit the performance impact) before
 handing them to the drawing context, so the GPU process only reads from memory
 it exclusively owns.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/commit/3e59292b95de1c22169fc939999ddd84d746319e
Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=308248
Author: Zak Ridouh <zakr@apple.com>
Last-Update: 2026-09-08
---
--- a/Source/WebKit/GPUProcess/graphics/RemoteDisplayListRecorder.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/GPUProcess/graphics/RemoteDisplayListRecorder.cpp
@@ -412,7 +412,9 @@ void RemoteDisplayListRecorder::drawGlyph
         return;
     }

-    context().drawGlyphs(*font, glyphsAdvances.span<0>(), Vector<GlyphBufferAdvance>(glyphsAdvances.span<1>()), localAnchor, fontSmoothingMode);
+    Vector<GlyphBufferGlyph, 128> glyphs { glyphsAdvances.span<0>() };
+    Vector<GlyphBufferAdvance, 128> advances { glyphsAdvances.span<1>() };
+    context().drawGlyphs(*font, glyphs.span(), advances.span(), localAnchor, fontSmoothingMode);
 }

