Description: CVE-2024-4367 - Fix missing type check on PDF.js FontMatrix allowing arbitrary JS execution
 A type check was missing when handling fonts (the FontMatrix) in the PDF.js
 renderer bundled by WebKitGTK/WPE WebKit. A malicious PDF could supply a
 crafted, non-numeric FontMatrix whose values were interpolated into a string
 that was then compiled and executed via eval()/new Function() in the font
 loader (getPathGenerator), yielding attacker-controlled JavaScript execution
 in the PDF.js context when isEvalSupported=true (the default).
 .
 This backports the upstream pdf.js fix (PR #18015, commit 551e639) to
 WebKitGTK's vendored copy of PDF.js. Per Source/ThirdParty/pdfjs/README.webkit,
 WebKit does not vendor the modular pdf.js source tree (src/core, src/display,
 src/shared, ...); it ships upstream's prebuilt, non-minified "dist" bundles
 instead, at Source/ThirdParty/pdfjs/build/pdf.mjs (main-thread/display code)
 and Source/ThirdParty/pdfjs/build/pdf.worker.mjs (worker/core code). This
 patch therefore applies the equivalent changes to those two bundled files:
  * pdf.worker.mjs (core/evaluator.js equivalent): validate the FontMatrix
    read from the font dictionary (must be an Array of exactly 6 numbers)
    and fall back to FONT_IDENTITY_MATRIX otherwise.
  * pdf.worker.mjs (core/font_renderer.js equivalent): emit glyph drawing
    instructions as a flat, numeric opcode/argument stream (FontRenderOps)
    via a new Commands helper that coerces any non-number argument to 0,
    instead of pushing string-command objects.
  * pdf.worker.mjs and pdf.mjs (shared/util.js equivalent): add the
    FontRenderOps opcode enum, exported from pdf.mjs's shared-util module.
  * pdf.mjs (display/font_loader.js equivalent): replace the
    eval()/new Function() glyph compiler with a switch over the numeric
    FontRenderOps opcodes that builds an array of closures, removing
    string-based code generation entirely; drop the isEvalSupported font
    path.
  * pdf.mjs (display/api.js equivalent): stop threading isEvalSupported
    into the font loader.
 .
 Verified: extracted the actual pdf.mjs/pdf.worker.mjs shipped in the
 2.50.6 orig source tarball, applied these edits, confirmed `node --check`
 passes on both files, confirmed this patch applies cleanly with `patch -p1`
 from a fresh extraction, and confirmed no eval()/new Function() call remains
 reachable from font glyph-path compilation (the only remaining new Function()
 use in pdf.worker.mjs is the unrelated PDF content-stream Function/calculator
 JIT, which upstream intentionally left using isEvalSupported).
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/mozilla/pdf.js/commit/551e63901c4e19450673c4832ef2235cf8f2fffa
Bug: https://github.com/mozilla/pdf.js/pull/18015
