Description: CVE-2026-28946 - Use-After-Free in BaseDateAndTimeInputType::didChangeValueFromControl
 A use-after-free could occur when the input type of a date/time form control
 was changed during dispatch of an input event fired from an editable date/time
 field. The DateTimeEditElement invoked callbacks on its edit-control owner
 (BaseDateAndTimeInputType) through a raw WeakPtr; if the owner was destroyed
 re-entrantly during one of those callbacks (for example when script changed
 input.type from within the "input" handler), subsequent accesses dereferenced
 freed memory.
 .
 This fix makes DateTimeEditElementEditControlOwner reference-counted
 (AbstractRefCountedAndCanMakeWeakPtr) and takes a strong RefPtr to the owner
 before invoking any owner callback, keeping it alive for the duration of the
 call. BaseDateAndTimeInputType forwards ref()/deref() to InputType. The null
 element case in setupDateTimeChooserParameters is also handled gracefully
 instead of asserting.
 .
 Backported from upstream commit 869d5c55313783da5714584b7db649435dbb16b0.
 The upstream hunks for defaultEventHandler (space key forwarding) and the
 didFieldOwnerTransferFocusToPicker/didSuppressBlurDueToPickerFocusTransfer
 owner callbacks are omitted because those code paths do not exist in this
 target version; the remaining owner-callback sites are hardened identically.
 WeakPtr-to-RefPtr uses .get() because webkit2gtk 2.50.6 lacks the RefPtr(WeakPtr)
 constructor present on upstream main.
