Description: CVE-2026-28905 - Fix classic buffer overflow via unwritten slots in FTL OSR array materialization
 Processing maliciously crafted web content may lead to an unexpected
 process crash (CWE-120, potential RCE). When a PhantomNewArrayWithButterfly
 is materialized during an FTL OSR exit, array slots that were conditionally
 not written before the exit point must be treated as holes. The previous
 code passed such empty (uninitialized) JSValues straight to
 putDirectIndex(), corrupting the array butterfly. Fix
