Description: CVE-2026-43731 - Fix UAF/write-after-unmap race in UserMediaCaptureManagerProxy
 A compromised WebContent process can send StartProducingData repeatedly for
 the same source. After the first call, the source proxy is registered as an
 AudioSampleObserver and the capture unit is invoking audioSamplesAvailable()
 on a background WorkQueue. On subsequent calls, prepareAudioDescription()
 runs on the GPU main thread and reassigns m_captureSemaphore, m_ringBuffer,
 m_audioHandle and m_description without removing the observer or taking any
 lock, while the capture thread is concurrently dereferencing them. This leads
 to heap-use-after-free on the freed ProducerSharedCARingBuffer / IPC::Semaphore
 and write-after-unmap into the old SharedMemory ring buffer (CWE-416).
 .
 Make UserMediaCaptureManagerProxySourceProxy::start() a no-op when the proxy
 is already observing media. Legitimate stop()/start() sequences are unaffected
 since stop() removes the observer. This is a hand-crafted backport of the
 isolable re-entrancy guard from the upstream fix, adapted to the 2.50.6 code
 base (the full upstream commit does not cherry-pick cleanly onto 2.50.6 due to
 unrelated churn in the same file); m_isObservingMedia already exists as a
 member in the target, so no new state is introduced.
 .
 A regression LayoutTest is added under LayoutTests/ipc/ that repeatedly sends
 StartProducingData for the same capture source; the test passes if the
 GPUProcess does not crash.
Origin: backport, https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/commit/b577b7842a1f7aa6283503ef0bee37be300cf80c
Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=314115
Author: Eric Carlson <eric.carlson@apple.com>
