Description: CVE-2026-28947 false positive — InstanceAnchor absent in webkit2gtk 2.50.6
 Documentation-only placeholder for Debian bookworm. The UAF lives in
 Wasm::InstanceAnchor teardown during JSWebAssemblyInstance destruction
 (WebKit bug 310234). That type and m_anchor were introduced after the
 2.50 branch point and are not in 2.50.6.
Origin: not-applicable
Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=310234
Author: Root.io <security@root.io>
Last-Update: 2026-09-17

--- /dev/null
+++ b/ROOT-SECURITY-RELEASE-CVE-2026-28947.md
@@ -0,0 +1,71 @@
+# CVE-2026-28947 — False positive for Debian 12 (bookworm) webkit2gtk 2.50.6
+
+| Field | Value |
+|---|---|
+| **CVE ID** | CVE-2026-28947 |
+| **Component** | webkit2gtk |
+| **Distribution** | Debian 12 (bookworm) |
+| **Package version** | `webkit2gtk` `2.50.6-1~deb12u2` |
+| **WebKit bug** | 310234 |
+| **Upstream fix** | WebKitGTK / WPE 2.52.4 (`76b34686210f`) |
+| **Assessment** | **FALSE POSITIVE — package is not vulnerable, no code patch required.** |
+
+## What the CVE is
+
+A use-after-free in JSC WebAssembly instance teardown. `Wasm::InstanceAnchor`
+can expose a `JSWebAssemblyInstance*` to other threads (including the
+compiler). If instance destruction starts while that pointer is still live,
+those threads use freed memory.
+
+The fix (`76b34686210f`, *Wasm::InstanceAnchor should be unregistered at the
+prologue of JSWebAssemblyInstance destructor*) tears the anchor down before
+any other destructor work.
+
+## Why 2.50.6 is not affected
+
+`Wasm::InstanceAnchor` / `m_anchor` were introduced in
+`f9f1ed183bf7` (`300108@main`, 2025-09-17). WebKitGTK 2.50.6 is
+`298234.491@webkitglib/2.50`, which predates that commit.
+
+On the `webkitgtk-2.50.6` tree:
+
+- `Source/JavaScriptCore/wasm/WasmInstanceAnchor.h` does not exist
+- `JSWebAssemblyInstance` has no `m_anchor`, `registerAnchor()`, or
+  `tearDown()`
+- `~JSWebAssemblyInstance()` only clears call ICs, import functions, and
+  tables — there is no anchor to unregister
+
+```
+$ test -f Source/JavaScriptCore/wasm/WasmInstanceAnchor.h && echo present || echo absent
+absent
+
+$ grep -nE 'm_anchor|InstanceAnchor|registerAnchor' \
+    Source/JavaScriptCore/wasm/js/JSWebAssemblyInstance.{h,cpp}
+# no matches
+```
+
+The 310234 patch has nowhere to apply. This is `vulnerable_code_not_present`,
+not a failed backport.
+
+## Tracker noise
+
+Debian, OSV, and WSA-2026-0003 list “WebKitGTK before 2.52.4” as affected.
+That is the version that *shipped* the fix, not a statement that 2.50 contains
+`InstanceAnchor`. Bookworm remains `<end-of-life>` / unfixed on the tracker
+for policy reasons, not because this UAF exists in 2.50.6.
+
+Do not confuse with CVE-2026-28946 (bug 310544), which is a different UAF
+and is patched separately on this package.
+
+## Verdict
+
+Mark as `not_affected` / `vulnerable_code_not_present`. This dummy patch only
+adds documentation; it does not change WebKit.
+
+## References
+
+- Fix: https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/commit/76b34686210f4f6779053590e7b9cfb1eadf6a15
+- Feature introduction: https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/commit/f9f1ed183bf72d7d7e5f17a5d4929845a302def2
+- Advisory: https://webkitgtk.org/security/WSA-2026-0003.html
+- Debian tracker: https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-28947
+- Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=310234
